{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0FXQ", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dab662cd95255d7968b9e820db3782b75c9895cb68d246f03a9e2a9cfb0e29ba", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA short section on the notion of a family of ample invertible modules.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2a3ef0ea45df6cc193ac6cab58719e93308f40603a305a138f0ffa7780a303d8", "unit_id": "tag:0FXQ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0FXQ", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[II Definition 2.2.4]{SGA6}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{\\mathcal{L}_i\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{\\mathcal{L}_i\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0008": "$i \\in I$", "MATH_0009": "$n \\geq 1$", "MATH_0010": "$s \\in \\Gamma(X, \\mathcal{L}_i^{\\otimes n})$", "MATH_0011": "$x \\in X_s$", "MATH_0012": "$X_s$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-family-ample-invertible-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d77225f5e7a386d9009838aa5c579cb148ab59272c4a8c1b38e93057fb54837d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:82bc72753db8136ea79d5362451722c2c6644c6ce4e38fe93348673832439102", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a family of invertible <MATH_0003>-modules. We say\n<MATH_0004> is an\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>ample family of invertible modules on <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0006> is quasi-compact, and\n<STRUCT_0003> for every <MATH_0007> there exists an <MATH_0008>, an <MATH_0009>,\nand <MATH_0010> such\nthat <MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012> is affine.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:200b20946b7bc2602df941759ac4948e3d01a6c5a2433b584c38e3b3a9d0a602", "unit_id": "tag:0FXR:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0FXQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\{\\mathcal{L}_i\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$I' \\subset I$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{\\mathcal{L}_i\\}_{i \\in I'}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:215cfbbe7c09a8a4a167f2928f10e03b9052cd256b842886669f5254e8c18bff", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b712a2ad248d1957dc8b7822663d0dc50c73ab6f6ee1dabf8b4320b540c3fe96", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIf <MATH_0001> is an ample family of invertible\nmodules on a scheme <MATH_0002>, then there exists a finite subset <MATH_0003> such\nthat <MATH_0004> is an ample family of invertible\nmodules on <MATH_0005> (follows immediately from quasi-compactness).\nA scheme having an ample family of invertible modules has an affine\ndiagonal by the next lemma and hence is a fortiori quasi-separated.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f07b41bcf2ee11d82bf18e04decad710d4394601254e630ae494f11b0c93b60", "unit_id": "tag:0FXQ:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0FXQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0005": "$s \\in \\Gamma(X, \\mathcal{L})$", "MATH_0006": "$x \\in X_s$", "MATH_0007": "$X_s$", "MATH_0008": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-affine-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:831de6c1d8292ac9ff3c7eb0421467d40420e6c608dc77760cbd4bf77e6fa09f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c440dd5b2d0f51f23c971bd6a2047a341f9a48a218b003e012b221b99ec8eea9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme such that for every point <MATH_0002> there exists\nan invertible <MATH_0003>-module <MATH_0004> and a global\nsection <MATH_0005> such that <MATH_0006> and\n<MATH_0007> is affine. Then the diagonal of <MATH_0008> is an affine morphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:11ffb04392acc6a86a8d04f51e948684f1cf2d3d906eb53424cc0ea5a1129179", "unit_id": "tag:0FXS:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0FXQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{M}$", "MATH_0004": "$s \\in \\Gamma(X, \\mathcal{L})$", "MATH_0005": "$t \\in \\Gamma(X, \\mathcal{M})$", "MATH_0006": "$X_s$", "MATH_0007": "$X_t$", "MATH_0008": "$X_s \\cap X_t$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Delta : X \\to X \\times X$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Delta^{-1}(X_s \\times X_t) = X_s \\cap X_t$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0012": "$X_s \\cap X_t$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{properties-lemma-affine-cap-s-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:149b02473b88827dc93b26f227c2b0e3a3d4da4b2d746ac91ad75548073a867e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:49f82e086612b0ac512b12c984fd8fd79dd79f67406924304427890220538439", "source_text": "Given invertible <MATH_0001>-modules <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003>\nand global sections <MATH_0004>,\n<MATH_0005> such that <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007> are affine\nwe have to prove <MATH_0008> is affine. Namely, then\nLemma <REF_0001>\napplied to <MATH_0009> and the fact that\n<MATH_0010> shows that <MATH_0011>\nis affine. The fact that <MATH_0012> is affine follows from\nProperties, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7a1e148056f047b7c146179136e3febb3347e950cc97a730d2528189e65468f9", "unit_id": "tag:0FXS:proof"}
